1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,450
Stop doing the busywork.

2
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:04,849
Keep control of your files.

3
00:00:04,849 --> 00:00:11,300
Every developer battles cluttered downloads, untracked duplicates, and messy workspace chaos.

4
00:00:11,427 --> 00:00:16,128
Meet SlothDesk AI: a calm, local-first productivity workbench...

5
00:00:16,128 --> 00:00:21,077
...that prepares inspectable proposals while keeping you firmly in control.

6
00:00:21,219 --> 00:00:25,919
Point SlothDesk to an authorized directory and launch a dry-run scan.

7
00:00:25,919 --> 00:00:29,119
In milliseconds, files are inventoried.

8
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:35,119
Streaming SHA-256 hashing detects cryptographic duplicates without silent deletion...

9
00:00:35,119 --> 00:00:41,069
...while grounded NLP extracts tasks, decisions, and deadlines with exact line numbers.

10
00:00:41,211 --> 00:00:47,911
In Automation Studio, four verified recipes turn routine file triage into dry-run previews...

11
00:00:47,911 --> 00:00:51,311
...with future tools clearly marked for version zero point two.

12
00:00:51,311 --> 00:00:56,561
The rule is simple: AI proposes, but nothing executes until you say so.

13
00:00:56,692 --> 00:01:02,391
In the Review Center, every proposed file move is staged with explicit paths.

14
00:01:02,391 --> 00:01:06,091
You select which operations to approve.

15
00:01:06,091 --> 00:01:08,391
Need to undo?

16
00:01:08,391 --> 00:01:14,491
A single click triggers tamper-resistant rollback, restoring files byte-for-byte.

17
00:01:14,619 --> 00:01:20,019
CSV Lab profiles tabular data deterministically in pure TypeScript—

18
00:01:20,019 --> 00:01:25,019
surfacing row counts, duplicate entries, and data types with zero cloud leaks.

19
00:01:25,019 --> 00:01:32,819
Under Settings, transparent diagnostics disclose whether Gemma or our fallback engine is running.

20
00:01:32,979 --> 00:01:37,379
Built for Hacktoberfest Week Three: Slow and Steady.

21
00:01:37,379 --> 00:01:43,379
Explore the live web demo on Render, run the workbench locally, and make automation safer.

22
00:01:43,379 --> 00:01:46,429
SlothDesk AI: calm automation.
